            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention is directed to a method (600) for manufacturing a shoe sole from randomly arranged particles (610) of an expanded material, comprising:a. positioning of a functional element (640) within a mold, andb. loading the mold with the particles of the expanded material,c. wherein the loading occurs through at least two openings (625; 635) within the mold,d. wherein one (635) of the at least two openings is arranged in a top part (630) of the mold and another one (625) of the at least two openings is arranged in a bottom part (620) of the mold, ande. wherein the particles of the expanded material surround the functional element from above and from below during loading.</p>
            </abstract>
